{{Quote|Sounds like that rough crowd out there is an easy one tonight.''"<br />"''All in a night's work, baby.|A Twi'lek dancer and Sy Snootles, after their performance for the Grand Hutt Council|<ref name="Hunt for Ziro">{{TCW|Hunt for Ziro}}</ref>}}
'''Sy Snootles''', also known as '''Miss Snooty''', was a [[Gender|female]] [[Pa'lowick]] singer and part-time [[bounty hunter]]. The former lover of [[Ziro Desilijic Tiure|Ziro]] the [[Hutt]], she [[Death|killed]] him on behalf of his nephew, [[Jabba Desilijic Tiure]], after Ziro abandoned her. Snootles was also a spy for the [[Hutt Clan]] and later become the lead vocalist for the [[Max Rebo Band]]. When it split up after Jabba's death, she resumed her solo singing career.

==Biography==
===Affair of the Fluid Sack===
{{Quote|I thought you were coming back for me. I waited so long. I thought you didn't love me anymore.''"<br />"''Our separation last time was a bit abrupt, and I do blame Jabba for that.''"<br />"''Jabba?''"<br />"''He forced me to have you sent away from Coruscant, shattering the serenity of the happiest time of my life.''"<br />"''Oh, Ziro, honey, being with you was the happiest time of my life too.|Sy Snootles and Ziro|<ref name="Hunt for Ziro" />}}
[[File:ZiroSyKiss.jpg|thumb|left|200px|Snootles kissing Ziro]]
[[Homeworld|Originally]] from [[Lowick]],<ref name="Updated and Expanded" /> Sy Snootles was a successful singer who dated [[Ziro Desilijic Tiure|Ziro]],<ref name="Ultimate Star Wars">''[[Ultimate Star Wars]]''</ref> a [[Hutt]] [[crime lord]] who represented the [[Hutt Clan]]'s business interests on the [[planet]] [[Coruscant]].<ref name="Ziro the Hutt">{{SWE|characters|zirothehutt|Ziro the Hutt}}</ref> However, according to Ziro, his nephew [[Jabba Desilijic Tiure]], forced him to send Snootles away from Coruscant, and while he promised to come back for her, he never did. A broken-[[heart]]ed Snootles<ref name="Hunt for Ziro" /> then became a [[spy]] for the Hutt criminal cartels<ref name="Sy Snootles" /> and part-time [[bounty hunter]].<ref name="Ultimate Star Wars" />

===Femme fatale===
{{Quote|Next time you'll think twice about breaking someone's heart. Oh, wait, there won't be a next time.|Sy Snootles before killing Ziro|<ref name="Hunt for Ziro" />}}
[[File:SnootlesShootsZiro-HFZ.png|thumb|right|250px|Snootles kills Ziro]]
In the [[Standard year|year]] [[21 BBY]],<ref name="Galactic Atlas">''[[Star Wars: Galactic Atlas]]''</ref> a vengeful Snootles was hired by Jabba<ref name="Sy Snootles SWE">{{SWE|characters|sysnootles|Sy Snootles}}</ref> to [[Death|kill]] Ziro and retrieve his [[holodiary]], which contained the [[Hutt Council records]]. After entertaining the [[Grand Hutt Council]] at [[Gardulla the Hutt's Palace]] on [[Nal Hutta]] with a lavish musical number, she discovered that Ziro was incarcerated in the palace's dungeon<ref name="Hunt for Ziro" /> following his [[Senate hostage crisis|escape]] from Coruscant's [[Republic Judiciary Central Detention Center|detention center]].<ref name="Hostage Crisis">{{TCW|Hostage Crisis}}</ref> Manipulating [[Gardulla Besadii the Elder|Gardulla]]'s [[Gamorrean]] guards into fighting each other, the Pa'lowick slipped her way past and to her estranged lover's cell. Exploiting her affection, they shared a kiss through the bars before Snootles broke Ziro out, the two escaping through the [[swamp]]s on a [[Pongeeta-class speeder|''Pongeeta''-class speeder]].<ref name="Hunt for Ziro" />

[[File:Jabba_receives_the_records.png|thumb|left|250px|Snootles turns over Ziro's holodiary to Jabba]]
Arriving at [[Mama]]'s [[Mama the Hutt's house|house]], Ziro convinced her to provide the pair with a [[starship]] to travel to [[Teth]], where his [[Papa|father]] was [[Tomb of Ziro the Hutt's father|buried]] and his holodiary, which the Hutt planned to sell so they could retire to [[Solarine]], was hidden. After retrieving it, a vindictive Snootles turned on Ziro and shot him twice in the chest. She then took his holodiary to [[Boba Fett's Palace|Jabba's Palace]] on [[Tatooine]], where the Hutt's nephew rewarded her handsomely for her services, while she boasted that nobody would suspect someone as "lovely" as her of being capable of doing a bounty hunter's work.<ref name="Hunt for Ziro" /> Neither [[Obi-Wan Kenobi]] nor [[Quinlan Vos]], the [[Jedi Knight]]s sent to recapture Ziro, ever found out that Snootles was the one who overtook them and murdered Ziro, allowing her to get away with her crime.<ref name="DD">''[[Dark Disciple]]''</ref>

In [[20 BBY]],<ref name="Galactic Atlas" /> a very tipsy Snootles, bottle in hand, was carried out of [[Bilbousa saloon]] by a pair of [[Twi'lek]]s.<ref name="Friends and Enemies">{{TCW|Friends and Enemies}}</ref>

===The Max Rebo Band===
{{Quote|Whoop! Uh-oh!|Sy Snootles watches Oola fall into the rancor pit|<ref name="Return of the Jedi" />}}
[[File:Sy_Snootles_Singing.png|thumb|right|300px|Snootles performs with the Max Rebo Band at Jabba's Palace]]
In the years that followed, Snootles turned her attention to her singing career. After meeting on board a [[luxury liner]], she and fellow singer [[Greeata Jendowanian]] became good friends and formed a performing duo. Having spotted them playing in a [[cantina]], the [[Ortolan]] [[Maximilian Rebo]] offered Snootles a place as lead vocalist in his [[Max Rebo Band]], which she only agreed to join on the strict condition that he also hired Jendowanian as a dancer and singer.<ref name="Updated and Expanded" /> She also became quite taken with fellow band member [[Droopy McCool|Snit]], whom she suggested change his name to the more palatable Droopy McCool,<ref name="Droopy McCool - Chindinkalu Flute Player">{{SWCT|set=Base Series 1|cardname=Droopy McCool - Chindinkalu Flute Player}}</ref> a stage name given to him by Rebo. She and her bandmates were outraged<ref name="Updated and Expanded" /> by Rebo's hasty decision to establish the band as a permanent attraction in Jabba's court,<ref name="Droopy McCool - Chindinkalu Flute Player" /> having immediately accepted the Hutt crime lord's offer of a contract that paid only in free meals.<ref name="Updated and Expanded" />

There,<ref name="Updated and Expanded" /> under the protection of [[Nizuc Bek]],<ref name="Force Collection">''[[Star Wars: Force Collection]]'' {{C|Card: Nizuc Bek (★★)}}</ref> Snootles worked as a double agent, feeding [[majordomo]] [[Bib Fortuna]]'s lies to Jabba's enemies.<ref name="Updated and Expanded" /> In [[1 BBY]],<ref name="Chronology note">{{BountyHuntDate}}</ref> Snootles, Rebo, and McCool were performing when [[Trandoshan]] [[bounty]] [[Bossk'wassak'Cradossk|Bossk]] arrived at Jabba's Palace looking for [[261]], a rogue [[Galactic Empire|Imperial]] [[astromech droid]].<ref name="Bounty Hunt">''[[Bounty Hunt]]''</ref> Shortly after the [[Assault on Cymoon|attack]] on [[Cymoon 1]] in [[0 ABY]], the trio was ordered out of Jabba's court when [[Sith Lord]] [[Anakin Skywalker|Darth Vader]] arrived to negotiate with the Hutt crime lord.<ref name="Vader">[[Darth Vader (2015) 1|''Darth Vader'' (2015) 1]]</ref>

In [[4 ABY]],<ref name="Galactic Atlas" /> the Max Rebo Band performed at a party in Jabba's Palace. Mistaking Jabba's advances on Twi'lek dancer [[Oola]] as a request for another song, Rebo began leading the ensemble through a variation on a popular standard, with Snootles belting out [[Jedi Rocks|improvised lyrics]].<ref name="Return of the Jedi" /> Her improvised lyrics were so saucy they embarrassed Bib Fortuna, and most likely would've been banned by the [[Galactic Empire]].<ref name="Star Wars: Return of the Jedi" /> Their performance was interrupted when Oola fell down a trapdoor, where she was devoured<ref name="Return of the Jedi" /> by [[Pateesa]],<ref name="Visual Dictionary">''[[Star Wars: The Visual Dictionary]]''</ref> Jabba's pet [[rancor]]. Shortly after, the group witnessed the bounty hunter [[Boushh]], in reality a disguised [[Leia Skywalker Organa Solo|Leia Organa]], enter the palace with the [[Wookiee]] [[Chewbacca]] as his prisoner. Later, Snootles watched as Jabba's guards captured Organa and [[Han Solo]] after Organa had freed Solo from the carbonite he had been encased in.<ref name="Return of the Jedi" /> The Max Rebo Band then accompanied Jabba's entourage aboard his [[sail barge]],<ref name="Updated and Expanded" /> the ''[[Khetanna]]'',<ref name="The Khetanna (Jabba's Sail Barge)">{{Databank|the-khetanna-jabba-s-sail-barge|The ''Khetanna'' (Jabba's Sail Barge)}}</ref> to view the executions of [[Luke Skywalker]], Han Solo, and [[Chewbacca]] at the [[Great Pit of Carkoon]].<ref name="Return of the Jedi" /> Although the sail barge [[Rescue of Han Solo|was destroyed]], the Max Rebo Band's members survived, but split up after Jabba's death. Snootles would find it hard to make it anywhere mainstream, chiefly because many found her vocals just too weird.<ref name="Updated and Expanded" />

==Personality and traits==
[[File:SySnootles-HuntForZiro.png|thumb|right|250px|Snootles was shrewd and ruthless underneath the guise of a sweet, innocent singer.]]
Sy Snootles was a [[Gender|female]] [[Pa'lowick]] with mottled [[Color|yellow]]-green skin, with blue spots. She had blue [[eye]]s and large red lips. Snootles wore a [[feather]] on top of her head and a skirt made of some strange material.<ref name="Star Wars: Return of the Jedi">[[Star Wars: Return of the Jedi (paperback novel)|''Star Wars: Return of the Jedi'' junior novelization]]</ref> She was considered a minor celebrity during her career. Although she was often viewed as an innocent person, she was shrewd, devious, and ruthless.<ref name="Base Series 1">{{SWCT|set=Base Series 1|cardname=Sy Snootles - Max Rebo Band Singer}}</ref> She did have some standards, though, as she expressed shock in horror the moment she saw Jabba drop Oola to her death, stopping singing upon witnessing the act.<ref name="Return of the Jedi" />

She was best friends with fellow performer [[Greeata Jendowanian]].<ref name="Base Series 1" /> Their friendship was so strong that Snootles only accepted being hired by Max Rebo on the condition he hired Jendowanian as a singer and dancer too.<ref name="Updated and Expanded" />

==Behind the scenes==
{{Quote|Sy was originally a classic marionette, performed from a scaffold overhead. However, she was about five-and-a-half feet tall, very heavy, weighing about sixty pounds. I redesigned her as a suspended, reverse string marionette.|[[Tim Rose]] on the design of Snootles for ''Return of the Jedi''.|<ref name="Insider222">{{InsiderCite|222|Inside the Mind of the Puppetmaster}}</ref>}}
[[File:SySnootles-BaseSeries1.png|thumb|left|250px|The Sy Snootles puppet]]
Sy Snootles first appeared in {{Film|VI}}. [[Phil Tippett]] described Snootles as "an egg on stilts." The character's big red lips were a suggestion from Executive Producer [[George Lucas]], who saw the marionette in the behind the scenes workshop and remarked that the character simply needed [[Wikipedia:Mick Jagger|Mick Jagger-style]] lips to complete her look.<ref name="Insider224">{{InsiderCite|224|Hit it, Max!}}</ref> Her puppet was designed<ref name="Insider222" /> and operated by [[Tim Rose]].<ref name="Insider224" />

For the "[[Hunt for Ziro]]" episode in the [[The Clone Wars: Season Three|third season]] of [[Star Wars: The Clone Wars|''The Clone Wars]] animated series, Sy Snootles was voiced by actress [[Nika Futterman]],<ref name=WoSW2023">{{SWCT|set=Women of Star Wars - 2023|subset=Signatures|cardname=Nika Futterman as Sy Snootles}}</ref> who provided the voice of the [[Sith assassin]] [[Asajj Ventress]] in the series.<ref name="Clone Wars Film">[[Star Wars: The Clone Wars (film)|''Star Wars: The Clone Wars'' film]]</ref> The episode first aired on [[November 12]], [[2010]], as the ninth episode of season three.<ref name="Hunt for Ziro Ep Guide">{{SWArchive|url=theclonewars/guide/episode309.html|text=''The Clone Wars'' Episode Guide: Hunt for Ziro}}</ref>

